      <p>The gap isn’t in the data itself—it’s in how it’s <strong>formatted, transmitted, and accessed</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- How Programming Bridges the Gap -->
    <section id="programming-bridge">
      <h2>How Programming Bridges the Gap</h2>
      <h3>🐍 Python</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Use libraries like <code>hl7apy</code> to parse HL7 v2 messages</li>
        <li>Transform messages into structured Python dictionaries</li>
        <li>Map HL7 segments to FHIR fields, output as JSON</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>📄 JSON</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Native to FHIR</li>
        <li>Easy to read, test, and validate</li>
        <li>You can version, diff, and mock FHIR resources in plain text</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>💻 JavaScript</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Build FHIR front-ends using frameworks like React</li>
        <li>Work with SMART on FHIR apps</li>
        <li>Use <code>fetch()</code> to call real-world FHIR APIs</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

